content.text:
Here’s what was wrong and what we changed.

**Cause:** `closePanelAndClearDrafts` only called `api.applyWizardDraftCompletion([])`, which updates drafts/vestiging maps but **keeps** `context`, `requestOrigin`, step-completion flags, `trajectServiceId`, informal intake fields, etc.

**Change:** Use the existing **`resetTrajectFlow(api)`** helper from `traject-submission-context.ts` (same as “Annuleren” on traject). It:

1. **`api.setFlowState(DEFAULT_ONBOARDING_FLOW_STATE)`** — full in-memory flow back to defaults (customer context, origin, flags, drafts, …).
2. **`clearOnboardingStorage()`** — drops onboarding flow, certification store, and registration-complete keys from storage so a refresh doesn’t resurrect old data.

Confirm copy was updated so users know registratiegegevens are cleared too.

```40:45:apps/frontend-pt1-extranet-onboarding/src/layouts/PublicCertificationRequestsCart.tsx
  const closePanelAndClearDrafts = () => {
    setOpen(false);
    resetTrajectFlow(api);
    navigate(WELCOME_PATH, { replace: true });
  };
```

Partial removals (`removeProductRow` when not the last item) still use `applyWizardDraftCompletion(nextDrafts)` only.

[REDACTED]

